-- title:
--   Finite étale level rings of the modular unit on X₀(p)
-- statement:
--   Let $p \ge 5$ be a prime, let $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldFull p` be the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \mathbb{Q}((q))$ (Laurent series) generated by the $q$-expansions $j(q^d)$ for the divisors $d \mid p$, and let $A =$ `Afin p` be the finite-$j$ chart subalgebra `chartAlgFin ℤ F (jFull p)` of $F$ of the two-chart integral model attached to $j$. Assume the modular unit series $\Delta(q)/\Delta(q^p)$ (formed as `deltaSeries` times the inverse of its $p$-fold $q$-expansion) lies in $F$, and let $v \in A$ be an element whose image in $F$ is either this series or $p^{12}$ times its inverse. Then there are a nonzero $\mathrm{avoid} \in (\mathbb{Z}/p)[X]$ divisible by $X$ and a nonzero $c_0 \in \mathbb{Z}[X]$ such that for every monic $g \in \mathbb{Z}[X]$ of degree at least $1$ whose reduction mod $p$ is irreducible and coprime to $\mathrm{avoid}$, and with $g \nmid c_0$ in $\mathbb{Z}[X]$, there is an integer $c \neq 0$ with $p \nmid c$ such that for every nonzero $f \in \mathbb{Z}$ divisible by $c$ the level ring $\mathrm{levelRing}\,p\,f\,v\,g = A[1/f]/(g(v))$ (the localisation of $A$ away from $f$, modulo the ideal generated by $g$ evaluated at the image of $v$) is a finite, étale, free module over $\mathbb{Z}[1/f] =$ `Localization.Away f`, of rank $(p-1)\deg g$, with rank at the stalk equal to $(p-1)\deg g$ at every prime of $\mathbb{Z}[1/f]$.
--
--   This produces, away from a finite set of primes, finite étale multisections of prescribed constant degree $(p-1)\deg g$ inside the integral model of $X_0(p)$, cut out by level sets of the modular unit $\Delta(q)/\Delta(q^p)$ (Ogg's unit) or of $p^{12}$ times its inverse. It supplies the étale "pools" used in [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_locallySplitPools_of_le_span_prime`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_locallySplitPools_of_le_span_prime), where such multisections must meet the fibre at $p$ in the smooth part of a single component.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_HpoolLevelRing_exists_finite_etale_levelRing_self.lean

